  "minimal_approach": [
    "Keep current SkillRecord/comprehension guards unchanged.",
    "Treat ASR-derived alignment, tentative words and recognizer failures as unassessed observation data; never map them automatically to parent weaknesses/errorPatterns. Exclude initial no-measurement zero summaries from competence interpretation.",
    "Propagate a typed text/finality/provider-status/optional-confidence result; error or uncertain results should request retry, not finalize partial data as assessed reading. High recognizer confidence alone still does not prove a reading weakness.",
    "If practice observations are retained, allow a corrected sentence/explicit confirmation to replace or clear its derived word set instead of union-only retention.",
    "Add one targeted existing-fixture regression across ReadingContent→ReadingProgressRepository→ParentReportEngine for partial+provider error, unclear text and correction. This is a recommendation, not an executed test or authorized product patch."
  ],
  "separate_profile_boundary": {
    "observed": "ReadingProgressRepository calls SharedPreferences.getInstance with lumo_reading_sessions_v1; summaries include childId, but ParentReportCard currently passes the full loaded list without child filtering.",
    "scope": "Concrete read path, not inferred merely from an unsuffixed key. No new two-child/device claim; separate scoping risk can be addressed independently."
  },
